{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1526908551,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDY1MDU4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2512#issuecomment-390650582"},"message":"Sounds like a good idea... but I wonder if that shouldn't be done automagically since cmdline invocation for a tool might have `{...}` in it?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1526911061,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDY2MTE3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2512#issuecomment-390661172"},"message":"Yeah, that's quite close to the syntax used in Snakemake:\n\nWith inputs of \"a\" and \"b\", `{inputs}` -\u003e \"a b\" and `{inputs[0]}` -\u003e \"a\".  Same for outputs.\n\n\u003e such that run would transparently inject the (unexpanded) input and output specifications into the command list\n\nAssuming a non-compound (i.e., `shell=False`) command, injecting the unexpanded values will fail because the command won't be able to deal with the globs that used to be expanded by the user's shell.\n\n@yarikoptic:\n\u003e but I wonder if that shouldn't be done automagically since cmdline invocation for a tool might have {...} in it?\n\nYeah, that'd be a problem, though I'd say we should do it automatically and have a flag to disable it.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527748295,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY1NTIzMDE1Mw=="},"status":2}]}